+# #5935 T0 — predictive-display evidence-role semantics
+
+H: A bounded human-facing forecast card can keep OBSERVED facts, PREDICTED state, typed effect status and UNKNOWN fields distinct, invalidate forecasts on fresh contradiction, and never promote prediction into action/effect authority. A deliberately overconfident/mislabeled forecast must fail validation.
+
+T: Six frozen event traces from #5935 T0 (stable target; target moved after capture; delayed save ACK; partial/unknown effect; abrupt regime change; predictor miss) crossed with four presentations: DELAYED_FACTS, BOUNDED_FORECAST, FACT_TAKEOVER_PACKET and BAD_OVERCONFIDENT negative control = 24 rows. Standard-library-only, no participant/model/GUI/input/network experiment. One formal invocation after public source/input/gate freeze; separate independent audit.
+
+D: METHOD_PASS_SCOPED iff all 18 legitimate presentations validate, all 6 BAD_OVERCONFIDENT controls reject, observed/effect provenance is exact, contradictions invalidate bounded forecasts, fresh-inspection option exists, action/effect authority remains false on every row, auditor errors=[], and >=8 effective evidence mutations reject. Missing denominator/source/process evidence is STOP/HOLD. This cannot support H_PASS_SCOPED human benefit.
+
+C: Correct semantic typing does not prove people notice or understand it. Fact-only takeover packets may dominate forecasts. A predictor can be wrong while the presentation contract remains valid; forecast quality and role safety are separate.
+
+U: No participant comprehension, accessibility, decision time, real display rendering, live application state, model/provider, action authority, effect truth beyond frozen trace oracle, or production usability is measured. T1 requires separate consent/governance and is not authorized here.
-- 
2.54.0


